    title: "Black Panther Party Founded",
    summary: "On October 15, 1966, Huey P. Newton (24) and Bobby Seale (30), students at Merritt College in Oakland, drafted the Ten-Point Program: \"We want freedom. We want power to determine the destiny of our Black Community... We want full employment for our people... We want an end to the robbery by the white men of our Black Community... We want decent housing... We want education... We want all Black men to be exempt from military service... We want an immediate end to POLICE BRUTALITY and MURDER of Black people... We want freedom for all Black men held in federal, state, county and city prisons and jails... We want all Black people when brought to trial to be tried in court by a jury of their peer group... We want land, bread, housing, education, clothing, justice and peace.\" The Panthers practiced armed \"patrolling the police\" — then legal under California open-carry law. They also launched the Free Breakfast for Children Program, which at its peak in 1969 fed 20,000 children daily in 36 cities. J. Edgar Hoover called the Panthers \"the greatest threat to the internal security of the country\" and launched COINTELPRO to destroy them. Fred Hampton, 21-year-old Illinois chairman, was murdered in his bed by Chicago police on December 4, 1969.",
