    title: "Tupac Shakur Dies",
    summary: "September 7, 1996: Tupac Shakur — 25-year-old rapper, actor, and poet — was shot in a drive-by at the intersection of Flamingo Road and Koval Lane in Las Vegas after a Mike Tyson fight. He died September 13. No one has been convicted. Tupac was the son of Afeni Shakur, a Black Panther Party member who was pregnant with him during the Panther 21 trial (1970) — she represented herself and was acquitted of all charges. His godfather was Geronimo Pratt, BPP Minister of Defense, framed by the FBI and imprisoned for 27 years. His stepfather was Mutulu Shakur, imprisoned for his role in the 1981 Brinks robbery. Tupac's *To Live and Die in L.A.*, *Dear Mama*, *Changes*, *Keep Ya Head Up* — his music functioned as both commercial pop and political pedagogy. He sold 75 million records. His death, four years after the LA uprising and three years after the Million Man March, marked the symbolic end of the hip-hop generation's first wave — a generation that grew up in the immediate aftermath of the civil rights and Black Power movements and tried to carry their analysis forward in commercial music.",
