    summary: "February 26, 2012: Trayvon Martin, 17, was walking back to his father's fiancée's house in Sanford, Florida, after buying Skittles and iced tea from a 7-Eleven. George Zimmerman, a neighborhood watch volunteer, called 911 to report a \"suspicious\" Black male, then pursued Martin against the dispatcher's advice. Zimmerman shot Martin in the chest at close range. Martin died unarmed. Zimmerman was not arrested for 44 days, until national protests forced the case. July 13, 2013: A jury of six women (five white, one Latina) acquitted Zimmerman of second-degree murder and manslaughter. July 14, 2013: Alicia Garza, in a Facebook post titled \"A Love Note to Black People,\" wrote: \"Black people. I love you. I love us. Our lives matter.\" Patrisse Cullors commented \"#BlackLivesMatter.\" Opal Tometi built the digital infrastructure. The hashtag became a slogan, became an organization (the Black Lives Matter Global Network Foundation was formally incorporated in 2014), became a movement, became a global framework for thinking about racialized state violence. #BLM is the most influential political hashtag in history.",
