    primarySourceText: "FERGUSON UPRISING (2014)\n══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\nLocation: Ferguson, Missouri, US\nEra: Era 8: Contemporary\nCategory: State violence / political organizing\nSource Tier: Tier 3: African Scholars\n\nAugust 9, 2014: Michael Brown, 18, was killed by Officer Darren Wilson in Ferguson, Missouri (a St. Louis suburb). Wilson shot Brown 12 times. Brown's body lay in the street for four hours. August 10 onward: Ferguson erupted. The uprising lasted weeks and was met with militarized police — armored vehicles (donated by the Pentagon's 1033 program), tear gas, rubber bullets, LRAD sound cannons. The phrase \"Hands up, don't shoot\" — based on eyewitness accounts that Brown had his hands up when shot — became the movement's chant, even though later forensic analysis disputed this. November 24, 2014: The grand jury declined to indict Wilson. Ferguson radicalized a generation of activists and birthed the Movement for Black Lives (M4BL), a coalition of 150+ organizations founded in 2014 and formally launched in 2016. Ferguson also revealed the structural role of municipal fines-and-fees: the Department of Justice's March 2015 report on Ferguson documented that the city funded ~25% of its budget through tickets and fines disproportionately issued to Black residents. The protests in Ferguson catalyzed protests in Baltimore (2015, after Freddie Gray), Milwaukee (2016, after Sylville Smith), Charlotte (2016, after Keith Scott), and elsewhere — a 6-year arc that ended in the 2020 global uprising.\n\nPAN-AFRICAN BRIDGE:\nFerguson is the contemporary US counterpart to the Soweto Uprising (1976) — both were moments when police violence against Black youth triggered sustained collective resistance, and both produced a generation of organizers. → `soweto-1976` · `trayvon-2012`\n\nTHREADS:\n- the-body-as-battleground\n- economic-sovereignty\n- press-radio-counter-media\n\nSOURCE CITATIONS:\n- 3 (Wesley Lowery, *They Can't Kill Us All*) + 4 (DOJ Ferguson report, M4BL platform)"
