    title: "*Black Panther* Film",
    summary: "Released February 16, 2018. Directed by Ryan Coogler (then 31), co-written by Coogler and Joe Robert Cole, starring Chadwick Boseman as T'Challa / Black Panther. The film grossed $1.35 billion worldwide — the third-highest-grossing film of 2018 and the highest-grossing film by a Black director. The fictional Wakanda — an African nation that was never colonized and that had developed vibranium-based technology surpassing any Western nation — captured the Pan-African imagination. Kendrick Lamar curated the soundtrack album, which became a cultural document in its own right (featuring SZA, The Weeknd, Schoolboy Q, Anderson .Paak, Future, Jay Rock). The film's release was treated as a cultural event — Black audiences wore African-inspired attire to screenings, school groups organized field trips, and the film generated a wave of \"Wakanda Forever\" gestures. The film won three Oscars (costume design, production design, original score) and was the first superhero film nominated for Best Picture. Its popularity revealed the hunger for a positive Pan-African vision — and its limits (it was, after all, a Disney property about a monarchy) sparked useful critique from Black intellectuals including Christopher Lebron (\"'Black Panther' Is Not the Movie We Deserve,\" *Boston Review*) and Dru Jeffrey.",
