    title: "George Floyd Murdered + Edward Colston Statue Toppled",
    summary: "May 25, 2020: George Floyd, 46, was murdered by Officer Derek Chauvin in Minneapolis. Chauvin knelt on Floyd's neck for 9 minutes and 29 seconds — the final 2 minutes and 53 seconds after Floyd had lost consciousness. A 17-year-old bystander, Darnella Frazier, filmed the murder on her phone; the video went viral. May 26 onward: Protests erupted in 2,000+ US cities and 60+ countries. The protests were the largest mass movement in US history — an estimated 15–26 million people participated. June 7, 2020: In Bristol, UK, protesters — organized by the \"Countering Colston\" coalition — tore down the statue of 17th-century slave trader Edward Colston from its plinth in the city center, dragged it through the streets, and rolled it into the harbor at Pero's Bridge (named after Pero Jones, an enslaved man owned by a Bristol merchant). The statue had stood since 1895; multiple attempts to remove it through official channels had been blocked by the local council. The Colston toppling was a direct echo of #RhodesMustFall (2015, Cape Town) and the broader global statue-toppling moment. April 20, 2021: Derek Chauvin was convicted of murder — a rare instance of police accountability. The substantive demands of the 2020 uprising (defund the police, end cash bail, reparations) went largely unmet.",
